      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "How to use",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# Platform URL -> Chinese transcript (yt-dlp)\n\n> Paste the **page URL** in **Download Media (yt-dlp)**, not a direct\n> video-only CDN link. Douyin/TikTok/YouTube/Bilibili often serve separate\n> video and audio tracks; yt-dlp resolves both.\n\n## Before Queue\n1. Paste the share/page URL, for example `https://www.douyin.com/video/...`,\n   `https://v.douyin.com/...`, `https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=...` or\n   `https://www.bilibili.com/video/...`.\n2. `mode = audio` downloads the best audio and converts it to WAV\n   (recommended for transcription). `mode = video` merges best video+audio\n   into an MP4.\n3. If the page needs a login or is region-locked, export a Netscape\n   `cookies.txt`, put it in `ComfyUI/input`, and set `cookies_file`.\n4. The first transcription downloads the FunASR model weights.\n\n## Pipeline\nyt-dlp -> Load Media -> FFmpeg Extract Audio -> FunASR (paraformer-zh) -> Format Transcript.\n\n- Use a direct CDN/video URL only if it contains audio; a video-only CDN link\n  will still fail with \"has no audio stream\".\n- If a site extractor breaks, update yt-dlp:\n  `python -m pip install -U yt-dlp` in ComfyUI's Python.\n\n## Output\n`ComfyUI/output/transcribe/chinese_transcript_url.srt`\n\nChange **Format Transcript -> format** to `txt`, `json` or `vtt` as needed.\n"
      ]
    }
